      "title": "MotherSphere/nikke-pc-launcher-compromise.md",
      "summary": "Attackers modified four official JavaScript files on Level Infinite's CDN, which the NIKKE PC launcher loads, to pull in a loader from the domain insightjs.com. The loader fetched a LuaJIT payload that gave the operator a remote-control agent able to run commands, read files, take screenshots and steal saved passwords, cookies, tokens, SSH keys and crypto wallet data. Opening the launcher from October 23 onward could activate the agent on some launches, and the Google Play Games build was also affected. The modified files were replaced by Level Infinite on November 3 and 4, and the insightjs.com domain was suspended on November 5. Defenders should save launcher logs and the tbs_cache folder, check debug.log for k2f_chan, remove the persistence DLL and its registry key, and rotate credentials from a clean device.",
