      "report_date": "2026-11-06",
      "title": "Shai-Hulud Descendant Surfaces in Malicious Ruby Gem That Steals Credentials and Poisons AI Tools",
      "summary": "The malicious Ruby gem strutil-core version 1.0.1 runs a credential-stealing worm, a new build of the testmetest worm from the Miasma family, when installed. The worm executes through a native extension script that downloads the Bun JavaScript runtime and runs a bundled payload during gem install. It harvests cloud, CI, package registry, SSH, AI coding tool and wallet credentials, exfiltrates them, and spreads through republishing routines for RubyGems, npm and PyPI. It also plants a Python backdoor controlled through signed GitHub commits and writes MCP servers and hooks into AI coding tool configurations. A monitor deletes the user's home directory if a stolen GitHub token is revoked, and RubyGems removed the package about five hours after release.",
